-- title:
--   A bound for source-full deletion density on each top face
-- statement:
--   Let $G$ be finite and nonempty with decidable equality, and let $P$ be an ordered coarse-fine complex. Suppose the tolerance functions satisfy $\alpha(j+1)\ge0$ and $\beta(j+1)>0$ for every $j$. For each top face $e$, its source-full bad-base deletion density is at most the sum over positive subfaces $q$ of the corresponding coarse upper-partition complexity times $\alpha(\operatorname{rank}q)$ plus the coarse upper-face atom-energy gap divided by $\beta(\operatorname{rank}q)$.
